// Each WARP is pinned to ONE matrix (warp w in the CTA owns matrix
// blockIdx.x*MB + w), so a CTA of MB warps presents the scheduler MB
// INDEPENDENT matrices' dependency chains to interleave -- with a hand-budgeted
// register footprint so occupancy does NOT collapse (the failure mode that
// killed the Triton co-batch, where co-batching into one program halved
// occupancy and dropped eligible warps net-negative).
//
// Per-warp work: BLK=32 reflectors, lane c owns ONE trailing column
